# Minimal tcgen05 FP16 MMA on SM_100a

Based on the documentation provided, here's the minimal working code structure. Note: The page provides wrapper functions and conceptual layouts but not complete inline-asm sequences. I'm synthesizing from the described primitives.

## 1. Shared Memory Descriptor Encoding (64-bit)

From the source, descriptors encode address and layout. The helper uses `(x & 0x3'FFFF) >> 4`:

```c
// Descriptor bits (inferred from text):
// Bits 0-43:   base address (shifted >> 4)
// Bits 44-52:  leading dim / stride encoding
// Bits 53-63:  swizzle mode + control bits

uint64_t desc_encode(void* ptr, int stride_bytes, int swizzle_mode) {
  uint64_t addr = ((uint64_t)ptr & 0x3FFFF) >> 4;
  uint64_t desc = addr | ((stride_bytes & 0xFF) << 44) | 
                  ((swizzle_mode & 0x7FF) << 53);
  return desc;
}
```

## 2. Instruction Descriptor (i_desc) for FP16→FP32

From the spec table: dtype (acc)=FP32 at bit 4, atype (A)=BF16 at bit 7, btype (B)=BF16 at bit 10:

```c
// For 128×128 block, 2 CTAs (MMA_M=256, MMA_N=128):
uint32_t idesc = (1 << 4)      // dtype=FP32
               | (1 << 7)      // atype=BF16
               | (1 << 10)     // btype=BF16
               | ((128 >> 3) << 17)   // MMA_N=16 at bits 17-23
               | ((256 >> 4) << 24);  // MMA_M=16 at bits 24-31
```

## 3. Full Sequence: tcgen05 + mbarrier

```c
// Allocation (one warp only)
int tmem_addr[1];
if (threadIdx.x < 32) {  // warp 0
  asm volatile(
    "tcgen05.alloc.cta_group::2.sync.aligned.shared::cta.b32 "
    "[%0], %1;"
    : "=r"(tmem_addr[0])
    : "r"(256)  // allocate 256 columns
  );
}
__syncthreads();
uint32_t taddr = tmem_addr[0];

// Initialize mbarrier (one warp)
uint64_t mbar_addr = (__shared__ uint64_t*)&mbarrier[0];
if (threadIdx.x == 0) {
  asm volatile(
    "mbarrier.init.shared::cta.b64 [%0], %1;"
    :
    : "r"((uint32_t)mbar_addr), "r"(2)  // count=2 for 2 CTAs
  );
}
__syncthreads();

// Build descriptors for shared memory tiles
uint64_t a_desc = desc_encode(smem_a, LDIM_A, SWIZZLE_128B);
uint64_t b_desc = desc_encode(smem_b, LDIM_B, SWIZZLE_128B);

// MMA loop
for (int iter_k = 0; iter_k < K; iter_k += K_BLOCK) {
  bool pred = (iter_k > 0);  // predicate: zero on first, accumulate after

  asm volatile(
    "tcgen05.mma.cta_group::2.kind::f16 [%0], %1, %2, %3, %4;"
    :
    : "r"(taddr), "l"(a_desc), "l"(b_desc), "r"(idesc), "r"(pred)
  );
}

// Commit completion to mbarrier
if (threadIdx.x < 32) {  // one warp per CTA
  asm volatile(
    "tcgen05.commit.cta_group::2.mbarrier::arrive::one.shared::cluster.b64 [%0];"
    :
    : "r"((uint32_t)mbar_addr)
  );
}

// Wait for mbarrier (parity-based)
uint32_t phase = 0;
bool done = false;
while (!done) {
  asm volatile(
    "mbarrier.try_wait.parity.acquire.cta [%0], %1, %2;"
    : "=r"(done)
    : "r"((uint32_t)mbar_addr), "r"(phase)
  );
}

// Fence before reading
asm volatile("tcgen05.fence::after_thread_sync;");

// Load results from Tensor Memory (each thread loads 8×FP32)
uint32_t results[8];
for (int n = 0; n < BLOCK_N / 8; n++) {
  uint32_t row_addr = taddr + ((warp_id * 32) << 16);
  uint32_t col_addr = row_addr + (n * 8);

  asm volatile(
    "tcgen05.ld.sync.aligned.32x32b.x8.b32 {%0,%1,%2,%3,%4,%5,%6,%7}, "
    "[%8];"
    : "=r"(results[0]), "=r"(results[1]), "=r"(results[2]), "=r"(results[3]),
      "=r"(results[4]), "=r"(results[5]), "=r"(results[6]), "=r"(results[7])
    : "r"(col_addr)
  );
}

// Deallocate
if (threadIdx.x == 0) {
  asm volatile(
    "tcgen05.dealloc.cta_group::2.sync.aligned.b32 %0, %1;"
    :
    : "r"(taddr), "r"(256)
  );
}
```

## Key Points from Source

- "Allocation returns a base address stored in shared memory, which all threads then read."
- Address format: `taddr + (row << 16) | col`
- Phase-based mbarrier avoids resets between pipeline stages
- `tcgen05.fence::after_thread_sync` required between MMA and LD operations

