# tcgen05 FP16→FP32 MMA Minimal Implementation

Based on the blog post, here are the key components for a minimal single-CTA tcgen05 kernel:

## 1. Shared Memory Descriptor Encoding

```cpp
__device__ inline uint64_t desc_encode(int val) {
  return (uint64_t)(val & 0x3FFFF) >> 4;
}

__device__ inline uint64_t make_smem_desc(int addr, int height) {
  const int LBO = height * 16;
  const int SBO = 8 * 16;
  return desc_encode(addr) | 
         (desc_encode(LBO) << 16ULL) | 
         (desc_encode(SBO) << 32ULL) | 
         (1ULL << 46ULL);
}
```

The blog specifies: "leading byte offset (LBO)" is "the stride from the first column to the second column of the 8x2 tile," and "stride dimension byte offset (SBO)" is "the offset from the first 8 rows to the next 8 rows."

## 2. Instruction Descriptor (32-bit)

For FP16 inputs, FP32 accumulation with M=128, N=256:

```cpp
constexpr uint32_t i_desc = 
  (1U << 4U)                    // dtype=FP32 (accumulator)
  | (1U << 7U)                  // atype=BF16/FP16
  | (1U << 10U)                 // btype=BF16/FP16
  | ((uint32_t)BLOCK_N >> 3U << 17U)  // MMA_N
  | ((uint32_t)BLOCK_M >> 4U << 24U)  // MMA_M
  ;
```

## 3. Key PTX Instructions

```cpp
// Tensor memory allocation
asm volatile("tcgen05.alloc.cta_group::1.sync.aligned.shared::cta.b32 [%0], %1;" 
  :: "r"(tmem_addr_smem), "r"(BLOCK_N));

// MMA issuance (with pre-computed descriptors)
asm volatile(
  "tcgen05.mma.cta_group::1 [%0], %1, %2, %3, %4, %5;"
  :: "r"(taddr), "l"(a_desc), "l"(b_desc), 
     "r"(i_desc), "r"(pred), "r"(0));

// Commit with mbarrier signaling
asm volatile(
  "tcgen05.commit.cta_group::1.mbarrier::arrive::one.shared::cluster.b64 [%0];"
  :: "r"(mbar_addr) : "memory");

// Load from tensor memory (32x32b fragment, x8 elements)
asm volatile("tcgen05.ld.sync.aligned.32x32b.x8.b32 "
  "{%0, %1, %2, %3, %4, %5, %6, %7}, [%8];"
  : "=f"(tmp[0]), "=f"(tmp[1]), "=f"(tmp[2]), "=f"(tmp[3]),
    "=f"(tmp[4]), "=f"(tmp[5]), "=f"(tmp[6]), "=f"(tmp[7])
  : "r"(addr));

// Synchronization fence
asm volatile("tcgen05.fence::after_thread_sync;");

// Deallocation
asm volatile("tcgen05.dealloc.cta_group::1.sync.aligned.b32 %0, %1;" 
  :: "r"(taddr), "r"(BLOCK_N));

// mbarrier initialization and wait
asm volatile("mbarrier.init.shared::cta.b64 [%0], %1;" 
  :: "r"(mbar_addr), "r"(1));
asm volatile("fence.mbarrier_init.release.cluster;");

// Wait loop
__device__ inline void mbarrier_wait(int mbar_addr, int phase) {
  uint32_t ticks = 0x989680;
  asm volatile(
    "{\n\t"
    ".reg .pred P1;\n\t"
    "LAB_WAIT:\n\t"
    "mbarrier.try_wait.parity.acquire.cta.shared::cta.b64 P1, [%0], %1, %2;\n\t"
    "@P1 bra.uni DONE;\n\t"
    "bra.uni LAB_WAIT;\n\t"
    "DONE:\n\t"
    "}"
    :: "r"(mbar_addr), "r"(phase), "r"(ticks));
}
```

## 4. Shared Memory Layout

The post states: "each 8x16B tile must be **contiguous** in shared memory" for no-swizzle mode. For 128B swizzling (recommended), use "8x128B tiles" as contiguous chunks with internal 16-byte unit permutation.

## 5. K-Dimension Atom

"MMA_K is always 32 bytes" for FP16 inputs (two 16-byte slices per MMA operation).

**Critical reference**: The blog emphasizes that understanding "Core Matrices" as implicit 8x16B units is essential for correctly calculating LBO and SBO values.

