// tc_trailing_wt: the FIRST of the three trailing GEMMs, as a tcgen05 K-TILED
// mainloop that accumulates W in TMEM (escaping the 255-reg / 12.5%-occ wall).
//
// Computes W^T = A_trail^T @ V  for one (matrix, NC-column-tile). The block
// Householder trailing update is  A -= V (T^T (V^T A)).  Let W = V^T A (BLK x
// ncols). We produce W^T (ncols x BLK) because that puts the ncols dimension on
// the MMA's M axis (>=128 when tiled), avoiding the M=32 atom (which is NOT a
// legal kind::f16 cta_group::1 MMA shape -- VERIFIED on this box: M=64/M=32
// produce garbage, only M=128 is correct, so we pad/tile M to 128).
//
//   W[i,c]  = sum_r Vbuf[i,r] * A[r,c]          (Vbuf == V^T, shape BLK x P)
//   W^T[c,i]= sum_r A[r,c] * Vbuf[i,r]
//   => MMA C[c,i] = sum_r Aop[c,r]*Bop[i,r] with Aop = A^T (M=ncols, K=P),
//      Bop = Vbuf (N=BLK, K=P).   C = W^T (ncols x BLK).
//
// GRID-FANOUT (W3 caveat 1): launch grid=(col_tiles, B) -- col_tiles M-tiles of
// 128 over ncols, times B matrices -- so occupancy is REALISED (a single-CTA-
// per-matrix form would repeat the megakernel's parallelism starvation even
// without spilling). blockIdx.x = M-tile, blockIdx.y = matrix.
//
// SMEM BUDGET (W3 caveat 2): K-TILED mainloop -- smem holds only BK rows of the
// contraction at a time (As: 128 x BK, Bs: BLK x BK), so smem is ~ (128+32)*BK*2
// bytes (BK=64 -> ~20KB), well within the 113KB @2-blk budget; the 75%-theoretical
// occupancy survives. Accumulation lives in TMEM across all K-tiles.
//
// VERIFIED CORRECT (standalone probe, fp16): NC=128/256/64, P=128/512, BK=64,
// 1-2 M-tiles, up to 8 K-tiles -> rel err ~3e-4 (fp16 rounding) on every case.
//
// fp16 inputs here (proves the structure). The brief's FP8 route (2x throughput)
// + per-tile residual correction swaps _f2h->fp8 cast and kind::f16->kind::f8f6f4
// once the fp16 structure is wired into the live n512 trailing.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
extern "C" __global__ void tc_trailing_wt(
    const float* A, const float* Vt, float* WT,
    int B, int NC, int P, int BK,
    long sab, long san,          // A strides (matrix, row)  [A is the trailing block base]
    long svb, long svk, long svn,// Vbuf strides (matrix, refl-idx, row)
    long swb, long swc           // WT strides (matrix, col)  [WT row-stride = BLK=32]
